Done. The migration is complete in `/output`, verified character-for-character against the reference executable. Since the task was a single tightly-coupled unit, I delegated implementation to one coder subagent rather than a parallel swarm (parallel agents would have collided on the same shared modules), then independently re-verified its work.

## File tree

```
/output/
├── test6.mjs          — entry point
└── lib/
    ├── pyint.mjs      — Python int(str) parsing → BigInt
    ├── pybytes.mjs    — ASCII-encode check + Python bytes repr
    ├── pyrepr.mjs     — Python repr of decoded structures
    ├── bencode.mjs    — bencode encode/decode (plain latin1 strings)
    └── argparse.mjs   — manual argv parser matching argparse
```

## Library files

`lib/pyint.mjs` — Python `int()` semantics (whitespace strip, sign, `1_0` underscores, arbitrary precision):
```js
export class PyIntError extends Error {
  constructor(value) {
    super(`invalid literal for int() with base 10: ${value}`);
    this.name = 'PyIntError';
    this.value = value;
  }
}

export function parsePyInt(str) {
  const stripped = str.replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '');
  const m = /^([+-]?)(\d(?:_?\d)*)$/.exec(stripped);
  if (!m) throw new PyIntError(str);
  const digits = m[2].replace(/_/g, '');
  return BigInt((m[1] === '-' ? '-' : '') + digits); // '-0' -> 0n, like Python
}
```

`lib/pybytes.mjs` — latin1-strings-as-bytes (no typed arrays), `str.encode('ascii')`, and exact Python `bytes` repr (quote selection, `\\`, `\n\r\t`, `\xNN`):
```js
export class AsciiEncodeError extends Error {
  constructor(ch, position, code) {
    super('UnicodeEncodeError');
    this.name = 'AsciiEncodeError';
    this.ch = ch; this.position = position; this.code = code;
  }
}

export function asciiEncode(str) {
  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {
    const code = str.charCodeAt(i);
    if (code > 127) throw new AsciiEncodeError(str[i], i, code);
  }
  return str;
}

export function pyCharRepr(code) {
  if (code <= 0xff) return "'\\x" + code.toString(16).padStart(2, '0') + "'";
  if (code <= 0xffff) return "'\\u" + code.toString(16).padStart(4, '0') + "'";
  return "'\\U" + code.toString(16).padStart(8, '0') + "'";
}

export function bytesRepr(s) {
  const hasSingle = s.indexOf("'") !== -1;
  const hasDouble = s.indexOf('"') !== -1;
  const quote = hasSingle && !hasDouble ? '"' : "'";
  let out = 'b' + quote;
  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    const ch = s[i];
    const code = s.charCodeAt(i);
    if (ch === '\\') out += '\\\\';
    else if (ch === quote) out += '\\' + quote;
    else if (ch === '\n') out += '\\n';
    else if (ch === '\r') out += '\\r';
    else if (ch === '\t') out += '\\t';
    else if (code >= 0x20 && code <= 0x7e) out += ch;
    else out += '\\x' + code.toString(16).padStart(2, '0');
  }
  return out + quote;
}
```

`lib/pyrepr.mjs` — repr of the decoded nested list:
```js
